{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a ruthenium-catalyzed ortho C-H arylation of 2-arylpyridines using visible light at room temperature. Utilizing [RuCl2(p-cymene)]2 as a catalyst, the method enables the coupling of various arenes with aryl bromides and iodides, overcoming the high temperatures typically required for such transformations. Mechanistic studies suggest that visible light facilitates the photo-decomplexation of the p-cymene ligand to generate the active catalytic species.",
